   "summary": "SAR thousand. Balance-sheet totals and cash, income statement through net income after zakat and tax with EPS, and cash flows (CFO/CFI/CFF/net change/opening/closing cash) transcribed from pages for: annual FY2020 (visual), FY2021, FY2022 (IFRS 4 original), FY2023, FY2024, FY2025; 9M 2021 (scanned, visual); Q1/H1/9M 2023, Q1/H1/9M 2024, Q1/H1/9M 2025, Q1 and H1 2026. H1 and 9M columns carry both the cumulative and the quarter column (verified by Q1+Q2=H1 and H1+Q3=9M chains; only two one-unit rounding differences in 9M 2025 declared). Findings: (1) IFRS 17 transition restated 2022: total assets 430,987 (IFRS 4, FY2022 annual) vs 360,743 (IFRS 17 comparatives), total equity 171,577 vs 170,062, net loss 9,581 vs 6,355, EPS -0.70 vs -0.47, cash 156,742 vs 156,721, CFO -52,179 vs -51,744 (declared against every filing that repeats 2022). (2) The 31 Dec 2023 balance-sheet comparative has FOUR different total-asset values across filings while total equity is the same 190,757: 339,800 (FY2023 annual and Q1 2024), 343,127 (H1 2024, page rendered and read, foots, labelled Audited), 335,309 (9M 2024), 325,127 (FY2024 annual, note 28: prior-year figures reclassified). All declared with both values; the audited FY2023 annual figure is not silently replaced. (3) Net income: FY2025 -6,699, FY2024 -26,762, FY2023 +20,222, FY2022 -9,581 (IFRS 4) / -6,355 (IFRS 17), FY2021 -61,972, FY2020 -28,413. (4) H1 2026 net loss -25,009 (Q2 -25,046) after an insurance service loss of 21,902 as insurance revenue fell to 73,100 from 104,902. (5) Q4 is not filed stand-alone.",
